NFR-01 — Accuracy

Character extraction and labeling must be highly reliable.

Target:

≥95% correct character extraction on clean template photographs.

NFR-02 — Robustness

The system should tolerate:

Different lighting
Slight rotation
Camera perspective
Moderate shadows
Different paper colors
Different handwriting thickness
NFR-03 — Performance

For a typical 4–6 page submission:

Processing should ideally complete within 30–60 seconds on a normal CPU machine.

Don't sacrifice extraction quality merely to achieve this target.

NFR-04 — Maintainability

Use modular components:

preprocessing/
alignment/
segmentation/
validation/
normalization/
vectorization/
font_generation/
preview/
packaging/
NFR-05 — Extensibility

Architecture must allow future integration of:

DINOv2 embeddings
Writer identification
Style embeddings
Few-shot glyph generation
AI-generated missing glyphs
Multiple handwriting styles
NFR-06 — Reliability

A failed character should not crash the complete pipeline.

The system should report:

D.png → invalid
E.png → valid
F.png → missing

rather than failing the entire job.

NFR-07 — Security

Uploaded files must:

Be type validated
Have size limits
Be processed in isolated job directories
Not be executed as code
Be deleted after configurable retention period
NFR-08 — Privacy

Handwriting is biometric-like personal data.

The system should:

Avoid unnecessary permanent storage
Delete uploaded images after processing when configured
Never expose one user's handwriting to another user
Keep generated files private
NFR-09 — Reproducibility

Given the same input pages and configuration, the system should produce substantially identical output.

NFR-10 — Observability

Every processing stage should produce structured logs:

JOB_CREATED
PAGE_PREPROCESSED
PAGE_ALIGNED
GLYPHS_EXTRACTED
VALIDATION_COMPLETED
FONT_GENERATED
JOB_COMPLETED